  4703                                      ;     The helper functions rtl8139_wr_d / rtl8139_wr_w silently fail on some QEMU
  4704                                      ;     builds for the CAPR/CBR pair (0x38-0x3B) even though they work for other regs.
  4705                                      ;     Use a direct 32-bit `out dx, eax` first (native dword I/O).  If that reads
  4706                                      ;     back as 0, fall back to FOUR 8-bit writes (one per byte at 0x38..0x3B).
  4707                                      ;     CAPR must be 0xFFF0 so QEMU sees the full RX ring as free, otherwise the
  4708                                      ;     60-byte ARP broadcast from SLIRP is rejected (needs 64+ bytes free space).
